        "name": "USN-9169-2",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - Stream parser;   - x86 architecture;   - GPU drivers;   - HID subsystem;   - I3C subsystem;   - MemoryStick subsystem;   - Network drivers;   - Ethernet team driver;   - NVME drivers;   - S/390 drivers;   - SCSI subsystem;   - Greybus lights staging drivers;   - Realtek RTL8723BS SDIO drivers;   - Thunderbolt and USB4 drivers;   - TTY drivers;   - USB Device Class drivers;   - USB core drivers;   - USB Gadget drivers;   - USB Host Controller drivers;   - USB Serial drivers;   - USB Mass Storage drivers;   - USB Type-C Port Controller Manager driver;   - TI TPS6598x USB Power Delivery controller driver;   - Ceph distributed file system;   - File systems infrastructure;   - F2FS file system;   - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;   - File system notification infrastructure;   - OCFS2 file system;   - SMB network file system;   - Kernel futex primitives;   - VLANs driver;   - Netfilter;   - TCP network protocol;   - Audit subsystem;   - BPF subsystem;   - Perf events;   - Watch queue notification mechanism;   - Memory management;   - Bluetooth subsystem;   - Ethernet bridge;   - Networking core;   - HSR network protocol;   - IPv4 networking;   - IPv6 networking;   - IUCV driver;   - MAC80211 subsystem;   - Management Component Transport Protocol (MCTP);   - Netlink;   - Open vSwitch;   - Packet sockets;   - RDS protocol;   - Network traffic control;   - SCTP protocol;   - SMC sockets;   - TIPC protocol;   - TLS protocol;   - VMware vSockets driver;   - Wireless networking;   - AppArmor security module;   - Key management;   - ALSA framework;   - Analog Devices audio codecs;   - USB sound devices; (CVE-2022-49622, CVE-2022-50167, CVE-2023-53733, CVE-2025-38728, CVE-2025-40135, CVE-2026-31678, CVE-2026-53353, CVE-2026-64015, CVE-2026-64190, CVE-2026-74341, CVE-